  "answer_text": "It looks like there are several different entities that go by the name **\"Chase Capital Services\"** or similar names. Here's an overview of the most notable ones:\n\n---\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfe6 JPMorgan Chase \u2013 Capital & Financial Services\nChase offers a broad range of services including credit cards, mortgages, commercial banking, auto loans, investing, and retirement planning. On the capital and investment side:\n\n- They provide tailored credit, financing, treasury, and payment solutions for businesses of all sizes and commercial real estate, backed by the strength and stability of J.P. Morgan, with dedicated experts delivering industry-specific guidance.\n- They help clients achieve long-term strategic goals through financing, liquidity, payments, risk management, and investment banking solutions, including M&A, capital raising, and risk management for corporations, institutions, and governments.\n- With J.P. Morgan Self-Directed Investing, customers get unlimited commission-free online trading in U.S.-listed stocks, ETFs, and options.\n\n---\n\n### 2. \ud83c\udfd8\ufe0f Chase Capital Holdings, LLC (Atlanta, GA)\nChase Capital Holdings, LLC is a trusted partner in investment real estate financing \u2014 a family-owned and operated boutique lending business based in Atlanta with 20+ years of expertise in the industry.\n\nTheir mission is to cater to the needs of experienced real estate investors throughout the Southeastern United States, offering quick and straightforward funding solutions for residential real estate investments.\n\n---\n\n### 3. \ud83c\udf41 Chase Capital (Canada)\nChase Capital is a private capital platform dedicated to investing in, advising, and helping unique businesses grow into dynamic platforms across Canada and other regions globally, bringing valuable capital and trusted industry expertise to acquisitions and partnerships with existing owners and operators.\n\nThey drive success in key growth sectors such as energy transition, waste & resource recovery infrastructure, and food & agricultural production, with a focus on investments and partnerships in the energy sector, supporting sustainable and innovative projects.\n\nUnlike traditional private equity funds, they invest their own capital and collaborate with a network of experienced entrepreneurs and investors, not bound by fixed exit timelines or rigid investment criteria, with a focus on building long-term, sustainable value.\n\n---\n\n### 4. \ud83d\udcc8 Chase Capital Partners (Now Closed)\nThis firm's broad platform positioned them to deliver extensive product capabilities \u2014 including lending, treasury services, investment banking, and asset management \u2014 to meet U.S. and international financial needs. However, Chase Capital Partners is permanently closed.\n\n---\n\nCould you clarify which **Chase Capital Services** you're referring to? For example:\n- Are you looking for **JPMorgan Chase** banking/investment services?\n- The **Atlanta-based real estate lending** firm?\n- The **Canadian private equity** firm?\n\nI'd be happy to provide more specific information!",
